<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n21932" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">impinguo</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">inp-</span></b> ), no <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>perf.</i>, ātum, 1,
				v. a. and n.
			in-pinguis. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>Act.</i>, <i>to make fat</i>
			(post-class.): impinguo <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πιαίνω,</span>
			Gloss. Philox.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">cui cor impinguatum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Tert. Jejun. 6</span></i>
			.—* </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>Neutr.</i>, <i>to become fat</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">porcellum tamdiu coques, donec lenis fiat et
					impinguet,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Apic. 8, 7, § 375</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
